# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
book/book
lab-out/
.superpowers/

# 10k author-time census output; committed charts come from census-lands-drift only
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-lands/
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-peoples/
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-faiths/
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-eyes/
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-tongues/
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-words/

# census-of-figures: a dev-time calibration instrument (night-sky stage 3,
# figure-threshold freeze), not a committed census fixture — the study json
# + metrics are committed, its rows.csv/summary output is not.
book/src/laboratory/generated/census-of-figures/

# Claude Code: project skills and shared settings (Bash timeout budget) are
# committed; personal settings.local.json and worktrees are not
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway census analysis database (tools/census/build.sh output)
tools/census/.build/

# The Casement: the .wasm is deploy-built, never committed (decision 0052);
# the wasm crate is outside the workspace so it has its own target/.
book/src/gallery/vessel.wasm
clients/vessel/wasm/target/

# The Lot: same discipline as vessel.wasm above (decision 0052) — built by
# `make wasm-lot` for the gallery's Lot exhibit (Task 10b, ledger #17); the
# wasm crate is outside the workspace so it has its own target/.
book/src/gallery/lot.wasm
clients/lot/wasm/target/

# perf/flamegraph captures (scratch — never commit; they hit GitHub 100MB limit)
perf.data
perf.data.old
*.perf

# The Ford probe (studies/the-ford-probe.study.json): a run-on-demand
# readout, deliberately not committed — same posture as the-pyx-probe.
book/src/laboratory/generated/the-ford-probe/

# The Gnomon's injection battery (studies/gnomon-injection.study.json): `lab
# run` publishes here, but the COMMITTED evidence is what
# scripts/gnomon-injection.sh copies into
# windows/lab/tests/fixtures/injection/ — this directory is the scratch it
# copies FROM, and the script deletes it after each arm. Ignored so a run
# cannot dirty the tree the script's own clean-tree guard reads.
book/src/laboratory/generated/gnomon-injection/

# The `pi` harness's per-machine working state — settings, npm scratch, and a
# workflow phase file (`"currentPhase": "execute"`). It is MACHINE state, not
# shared configuration: this checkout carries 62 such files while only three
# were ever committed, and two of those three differed from the local copy the
# moment they landed, so tracking them means every machine fights over them.
#
# Committed by hand in 54d4f9f44 and reverted here. Worth knowing HOW it
# reached main, because no local guard could have stopped it and none can:
# it was authored through the GitHub web UI (a `users.noreply.github.com`
# identity), and `scripts/hooks/pre-push` — decision 0139's enforcement — runs
# on the pusher's machine. A commit made in a browser never touches one.
.pi/

# macOS Finder metadata. Nathan works across a Mac and lefford, so these appear
# only on one side of the pair — which is exactly why they are easy to miss
# until one is committed from the machine that creates them. None is tracked
# and none is on disk as of 2026-08-29; this is preventive, not a cleanup.
.DS_Store

# Observation films and their local render inputs are derived review output.
# Manifests and small deterministic fixtures remain committed under observations/.
observations/render-output/

# Staging documents are per-effort scratch, never a shared tracked path.
# See CLAUDE.md (Process): a root IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md was one mutable path
# every campaign wrote, and a `cat >` over it clobbered a live campaign silently.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
